# SCSS is the source of truth

A compiler is running. **Never create or edit `.css` files.** Write styles only in the matching `.scss`.

- `src/styles/style.scss` → compiled `src/styles/style.css`
- `src/styles/site.scss` → compiled `src/styles/site.css`

Do not "keep CSS in sync." Do not patch both. If a `.css` file is open, still change only the `.scss`.

```scss
// ✅ GOOD — edit the SCSS
.scroll-hint {
	color: var(--green-dark);
}
```

```css
/* ❌ BAD — compiled output; the compiler overwrites this */
.scroll-hint {
  color: var(--green-dark);
}
```
